     "page": 1,
     "text": "Marsh Inc Medical Group\nRe: Lisa Lowe (DOB 09/16/1986)\n\nApril 27, 2026: Lisa Lowe presented today follow-up of her Heart failure / cardiomyopathy. She reports no new symptoms and is doing well. Her blood at this visit was 112/90, and her weight was 141 pounds. She continues on spironolactone 25 mg and carvedilol 6.25 mg. She has been stable on these medications for a while now, and her condition remains well-controlled.\n\nNovember 21, 2025: Lisa was seen for follow-up of her Heart failure / cardiomyopathy. She reports feeling well with no new symptoms. Her blood pressure was 104/87, and her weight was 141 pounds. She remains on spironolactone 25 mg and carvedilol 6.25 mg. Her ejection fraction is 52%, and she has been stable for approximately 4.1 years.\n\nJune 16, 2025: Lisa visited for a routine follow-up regarding her Heart failure / cardiomyopathy. She is feeling well with no new issues. Her blood pressure was 103/86, and her weight was 148 pounds. She continues to take spironolactone 25 mg and carvedilol 6.25 mg. Her ejection fraction remains at 52%, and she has been stable for approximately 4.1 years.\n\nJanuary 10, 2025: Lisa was seen for a routine visit related to a recent upper respiratory infection (URI). She reports feeling well now, with no persistent symptoms. Her blood pressure was 119/88, and her weight was 151 pounds. She also continues to manage her Heart failure / cardiomyopathy. Her medications remain spironolactone 25 mg and carvedilol 6.25 mg, and her ejection fraction is stable at 52%.\n\nAugust 5, 2024: Lisa presented for follow-up of her Heart failure / cardiomyopathy. She reports no new symptoms and doing well. Her blood pressure was 116/83, and her weight was 156 pounds. She is continuing on spironolactone 25 mg and carvedilol 6.25 mg. Her ejection fraction is 52%, and she has been stable for approximately 4.1 years.\n\nFebruary 29, 2024: Lisa was seen for routine follow-up of her Heart failure / cardiomyopathy. She reports feeling well with no new symptoms. Her blood pressure was 118/86, and her weight was 142 pounds. She continues on spironolactone 25 mg and carvedilol 6.25 mg. Her condition is stable, and her ejection fraction is 52%.\n\nSocial history reveals that Lisa consumes alcohol on occasion, approximately 2 drinks per week. This information is provided for a complete understanding of her lifestyle and habits.\n\nDr. Alison Bray\nMarsh Inc Medical Group\nCardiology\n"
