     "text": "RIVERA AND SONS CLINIC - DISCHARGE SUMMARY\nPatient: Lisa Lowe DOB: 09/16/1986 Sex: F MRN: 589540\nAdmit: 05/02/2023 Discharge: 05/05/2023\n\nPrincipal diagnosis: Eating disorder (recovered ~9.4 yrs)\nSecondary diagnoses: Heart failure / cardiomyopathy (EF 52%; recovered ~4.1 yrs); rosacea; musculoskeletal injury\n\nHISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS:\nMs. Lisa Lowe, a 39-year-old female, presented to the clinic on May 2, 2023, with a history of a musculoskeletal injury. She also has a medical history significant for an eating disorder, heart failure with cardiomyopathy, and rosacea. The patient reported no acute distress at the time of admission and was stable.\n\nADMISSION PHYSICAL EXAMINATION:\nVital signs on admission were stable. Blood pressure was 119/83 mmHg, and weight was 151 lbs. The physical examination was otherwise unremarkable except for findings consistent with her known medical conditions.\n\nHOSPITAL COURSE:\nMs. Lowe was admitted for evaluation and management of her musculoskeletal injury. During her hospital stay, she remained hemodynamically stable with no significant changes her vital signs. She received appropriate pharmacological treatment for her conditions. The hospital course was uneventful, and she showed good response to the therapy. There were complications or adverse events during her stay.\n\nDISCHARGE MEDICATIONS:\n1. Spironolactone 25 PO daily for heart failure\n2. Carvedilol 6.25 mg PO twice daily for heart failure\n3. Ivermectin topical 1% applied to the affected once daily for rosacea\n4. Metronidazole topical 1% applied to the affected area twice daily for rosacea\n5. Cyclobenzaprine 5 mg PO at bedtime for musculoskeletal injury\n6. Ibuprofen 600 mg PO every 6 hours as needed for pain associated with musculoskeletal injury\n\nDISCHARGE INSTRUCTIONS:\nThe patient was instructed to continue her medications as prescribed and to follow up with her primary care provider for further management of her conditions. She was advised to maintain a healthy lifestyle, including a balanced diet and regular physical activity, within her capabilities. She was also encouraged to avoid alcohol smoking.\n\nFOLLOW-UP:\nMs. Lowe is scheduled to follow up with Dr. Lauren Howell at Rivera and Sons Clinic in two weeks for a reevaluation of her musculoskeletal injury and overall health status. She is also advised to make an appointment with a cardiologist for continued management of her heart failure and cardiomyopathy.\n\nSOCIAL HISTORY:\nMs. Lowe reports consuming approximately 2 drinks per week. She denies any current use of tobacco products. Her family"
